 { This position was reached in Korchnoi,V - Antoshin,V (1966) . Which two-move sequence did White play in order to first create hanging pawns, and then immediately undermine them? } 15. { -KEY- } cxd5 exd5 16. b4 $1 { Correct! Now Black is forced to mobilise their hanging pawns along the light squares. } ( 16. e4 $6 { is another way of undermining the pawns, but much less convincing after } dxe4 $1 { since now White will be forced to accept an isolated pawn of their own on e4. } ) 
c4 17. Bc2 Nc6 18. Bb2 $16 { White stood much better due to his active bishops and excellent control of the dark squares. } 
