 { How should you recapture on e4? } 1. { -KEY- } dxe4 $1 { Correct! White accepts doubled pawns in order to create a semi-open d-file and secure a power outpost on d5. } ( { After } 1. Nxe4 $6 Qc7 $11 { Black is fine in spite of the backward pawn on d6, since there is no way for White to increase the pressure against it. } ) 
Be6 2. Qd2 Qe7 3. Rad1 Rad8 4. e3 $16 { The second e-pawn does an excellent job of taking away the d4 square from Black's knight. White stands better with more space and better long-term activity for their pieces. } 
