 ( { Should White play } 1. Nxd6 { or } 1. Na5 $2 ) 
1. { -KEY- } Nxd6+ $1 { Correct! It often pays to stay flexible and be willing to improve your opponent's structure for other positional advantages. } ( 1. Na5 $6 { The attempt to keep the pawn structure doubled does not work out well for White. } c5 $1 2. Qe3 Ng6 { Black has good coordination and central control, leaving them without problems in spite of having doubled pawns on the c-file. } ) 
cxd6 ( 1... Qxd6 2. Rd1 $16 { In this line Black maintains the poor pawn structure, while also having lost their valuable dark-squared bishop. } ) 
2. Rd1 $1 d5 3. Ba3 $16 { White stands much better due to their better-placed pieces and domination along the dark squares. } 
