 ( { Taken from the game Manca, F - Eisenbeiser, K (2005). Should White play } 15. d5 { (grabbing space) or } 15. dxe5 { (changing the structure)? } ) 
15. { -KEY- } dxe5 $1 { Correct! } ( 15. d5 $6 { Shutting down the centre is a bad idea. Black can play something like } Nh5 { to trade bishops, and in the future grab the initiative by breaking with ...f5. } ) 
dxe5 $6 16. Nbd2 $16 { Now White has a much better position, with the central pawn on e4 safely guarded and a beautiful outpost on c4 that may be used by the knight in the future. For anyone curious, the rest of the game is included without annotations. } Qc7 17. Nc4 Rfe8 18. Bxf6 Nxf6 19. Ncxe5 Rf8 20. Qd3 Rad8 21. Qc4 Bxe4 22. Rxe4 Nxe4 23. Nxf7 Rxf7 24. Qxf7+ Kh8 25. Re1 Rf8 26. Qe6 Rxf3 27. Qg8# { 1-0 White wins. } 
