 { Find the best sequence for Black. } 1... { -KEY- } Bc4 $1 { Immediately exploiting a typical feature of IQP positions: the vulnerability of the c4 square. In cases where Black is the side with the IQP it is the c5 square that is quite weak. } 2. Qh3 { The only way to avoid material losses. } ( 2. Qd1 $2 { This was played in the game, but Black can win an exchange after } Bxc3 3. Nxc3 Bxf1 $19 ) 
h6 $1 { Correct! Now White is forced to part ways with their bishop pair. } ( { But not } 2... Bxe2 $2 { , since now the Black king lands in some trouble after } 3. Bxf6 Qxf6 4. Qxh7 Kf8 5. Rae1 $11 { White will recover their bishop with approximate equality, since if Black withdraws it then White will play Qh7-h8 with mate. } ) 
3. Bxf6 ( 3. Be3 $2 Bxc3 4. Nxc3 Bxf1 $19 ) 
Qxf6 4. Bd3 Rad8 $17 { White has succeeded in avoiding decisive material losses, but Black has a big advantage due to the better placed pieces and favorable structure. } 
